 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "This, that, that",
   "texto": [
    "The Korean has three distances, like the Spanish. **이** (this): near me. **그** (that): near you. **저** (that one): away from both.",
    "Before a name: **이 책** (this book), **그 책** (that book), **저 책** (that book).",
    "Alone, when speaking: **이거** (this), **그거** (that), **저거** (that).",
    "When they are the subject of the phrase they are shortened: **이게**, **그게**, **저게**. So «What is this?» is **이게 뭐예요?**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "tabla",
   "titulo": "Three distances",
   "filas": [
    [
     "near me",
     "이",
     "이거",
     "이게"
    ],
    [
     "near you",
     "그",
     "그거",
     "그게"
    ],
    [
     "away from both of us",
     "저",
     "저거",
     "저게"
    ]
   ],
   "columnas": [
    "",
    "In front of name",
    "Alone.",
    "As a subject"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Whose is it?",
   "texto": [
    "To say «of» there is the **의** particle (it is pronounced «e»), but when speaking it is almost always removed: **민수 씨 책** = the book of Minsu.",
    "**누구** = who. **누구 거예요?** = whose is it? (h- = «thing.», «the»).",
    "**제 거예요** = is mine. **민수 씨 거예요** = is from Minsu."
   ]
  },
